        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-enhanced-a-polynomial-newton-polygon-detects-torus-knots",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC and let $K\\subset S^3$ be a smooth knot. For a nonzero Laurent polynomial $f(M,L)$, its Newton polygon is the convex hull in $\\mathbb R^2$ of exponent pairs $(a,b)$ for which the coefficient of $M^bL^a$ is nonzero. The enhanced A-polynomial is **thin** when this polygon is contained in an affine line; the constant polynomial $1$ has a one-point Newton polygon and is thin. Then the enhanced A-polynomial of $K$ is thin if and only if $K$ is a torus knot, including the unknot.",
          "uses": [
