          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-torus-knot-enhanced-a-polynomial",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC and let $a>b\\ge2$ be coprime positive integers. With the meridian-longitude and exponent conventions used for the enhanced A-polynomial, the enhanced A-polynomial of $T_{a,b}$ is, up to multiplication by a Laurent unit,\n$$\\widetilde A_{T_{a,b}}(M,L)=\\begin{cases}1+M^{2a}L,&b=2,\\\\-1+M^{2ab}L^2,&b>2.\\end{cases}$$\nIf $K$ is the unknot, then $\\widetilde A_K=1$. The nontrivial torus-knot Newton polygon is therefore a line segment whose slope in the $(a,b)\\mapsto M^bL^a$ convention is $ab$.",
