          "source": "thm-torus-knot-alexander-and-genus-formulas",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the full Axiom of Choice. Let $p,q$ be coprime nonzero integers, let $K=T(p,q)$, and put $a=|p|$, $b=|q|$. For $\\Lambda=\\mathbb Z[t^{\\pm1}]$, define\n$$\\delta_{a,b}(t)=\\frac{(t^{ab}-1)(t-1)}{(t^a-1)(t^b-1)}.$$\nThen $\\delta_{a,b}(t)$ is a polynomial in $\\mathbb Z[t]$, the Alexander polynomial $\\Delta_K$ defined as a generator of the zeroth elementary ideal of the positive-meridian infinite-cyclic-cover module satisfies $\\Delta_K(t)\\doteq\\delta_{a,b}(t)$, and the knot genus is $g(K)=(a-1)(b-1)/2$. Here $f\\doteq g$ means $f=\\pm t^k g$ for some integer $k$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
