          "source": "lem-figure-eight-character-and-longitude-traces",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC and let $K=J(2,-2)$ be the figure-eight knot. Use the two-bridge group presentation $\\pi_1(E_K)=\\langle u,v\\mid v w=w u\\rangle$, where $w=uv^{-1}u^{-1}v$, and take $\\mu=u$. On the one-dimensional irreducible character component, define $x(\\chi)=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho(u))=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho(v))$ and $y(\\chi)=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho(uv))$. Then\n$$2x^2+y^2-x^2y-y-1=0,$$\nand the preferred-longitude trace is $\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho(\\lambda))=x^4-5x^2+2$. The displayed curve equation is irreducible over $\\mathbb C$, and $x$ is nonconstant on it.",
