          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-finite-variable-polynomial-rings-over-fields-are-ufds",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $k$ be a field and let $r\\ge0$ be an integer. Then $k[x_1,\\ldots,x_r]$ is a\nunique factorisation domain ([[def-unique-factorisation-domain]]). Every\nirreducible element of it is prime\n([[def-irreducible-and-prime-elements-in-a-domain]]), and every prime ideal of\nheight one ([[def-height-of-a-prime-ideal]]) is generated by an irreducible\nelement.\n\nFor $r=0$ the ring is the field $k$ itself\n([[def-multivariate-polynomial-ring-by-iteration]]); it has no irreducibles and\nno height-one primes.",
